  "title": "DMK Party Revamp: Age Limits and Organizational Changes",
  "summary": "The Hindu National party announced revisions to its organisational structure, including setting age limits for district secretaries and local units, aiming to address staffing shortages in its governance framework. These changes are part of a broader effort to strengthen the party’s leadership and operational efficiency.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The DMK party set age limits of 45 for local units and 70 for district secretaries to enhance its structure and ensure representation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "M.K. Stalin, a prominent leader in the party, emphasized the need to address past performance and admit mistakes to improve the party’s governance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The proposal was adopted during a high-level executive committee meeting chaired by President Stalin.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
